  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;be an integer such that the triangle with vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> has area&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>28</mn></math>&nbsp;sq. units. Then the orthocenter of this triangle is at the point:"
  },
